{"resourceIdentifier":"4612","resourceName":"WEIYUAN COMPOSTING PROJECT","description":"Weiyuan Composting Project (hereafter referred to as the project) installs a set of organic fertilizer production lines with an annual capacity of 50,000 tons to treat swine manure from swine farms and biomass waste residue (straw) in Weiyuan County, Neijiang City, Sichuan Province, China. The project is invested and owned by Sichuan Zhengwei Industry Co., Ltd. The purpose of the project activity is to avoid methane emissions through controlled aerobic treatment by composting of manure and biomass waste residue. This project comprises of fermentation system and fertilizer production system. It is estimated that approximately 102,000 tonnes of manure and 35,000 tonnes of biomass waste residue can be treated annually, therefore total 137,000 tonnes of waste can be composted aerobically for this project. A portion of the organic fertilizer obtained is sold to the local government for improving the quality of local high-standard farmland, and another portion is sold to local farmers, farmer cooperatives and businesses. The construction start date of the project is 21 July 2020 and was put into operation on 1 January 2022. The project activity will reduce of GHG in the atmosphere through avoiding methane emissions from controlled aerobic treatment by composting of manure and biomass residue. It is estimated that 59,518 tCO2e emission reductions will be generated annually and total emission reductions are 595,175 tCO2e in the 10 years’ fixing crediting period.","location":{"latitude":29.586935,"longitude":104.674086},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2023-10-06","endExclusive":"2023-11-06","endInclusive":"2023-11-05"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"4612"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Sichuan Province"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code"